    x86_bootstrap_rust_authority_tuple_recompilation_cost_2026-08-22, 1, "2026-11-04 bootstrap triage (c): needs a working self-hosted stage3 to verify or repro; cannot be settled with the Rust seed bin/simple.exe. Exact steps: (1) fresh worktree rebased on origin/release/1.0.0 with no other bootstrap running; (2) SIMPLE_NO_STUB_FALLBACK=1 sh scripts/bootstrap/bootstrap-from-scratch.sh --full-bootstrap --deploy (sanctioned bootstrap; yields build/bootstrap/stage3/<triple>/simple and stage3-command.transcript); (3) replay the Symptom/Repro section of doc/08_tracking/bug/x86_bootstrap_rust_authority_tuple_recompilation_cost_2026-08-22.md with that stage3 binary under a timeout (stage3 cmd form: build/bootstrap/stage3/<triple>/simple native-build <entry> ..., or replay stage3-command.transcript) and capture rc plus last 50 log lines; (4) append the observed rc and log here and set status closed if it no longer reproduces."
    x86_bootstrap_rust_authority_tuple_recompilation_cost_2026-08-22, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep4: measured the doc's four-serial-invocation tuple on a frozen snapshot worktree with the bootstrap's exact env (gnullvm triple, llvm-mingw authority, isolated CARGO_HOME, vendored deps; cranelift backend since this host lacks admitted LLVM 23): cold total 1594s (seed 700s / native-all 509s / runtime-nolto 214s / backfill 171s). Warm rerun before fix: inv2-4 fully Fresh but inv1 recompiled simple-driver EVERY time - cargo -v reason: Dirty simple-driver: the file .../test/unit/lib/std is missing (a legacy path absent from the current tree; cargo cannot fingerprint a missing watched path). Fix: driver/build.rs:264 emits the test-root rerun-if-changed only when the root exists. After: warm inv1 pass1 73s/1 unit (one-time absorption), pass2 5s 0 units all Fresh; libsimple_driver.rlib sha256 byte-identical pre/post (simple.exe differs only by the pre-existing PE-timestamp link nondeterminism, separate open bug). Cold repeats are all admitted-identity-defining (fingerprint/cargo-tree/-v evidence preserved): inv2 seed-only mimalloc + cuda/native-all features; inv3 LTO-off runtime archive; inv4 smaller feature graph + different per-unit LTO roles - not removable without changing artifact bytes (vendored-manifest surgery, out of scope). Deliverables: pinning check scripts/bootstrap/tests/driver-watch-root-gate-test.shs (PASS) + new must_check_gates row local-driver-watch-root-gate + reseal. Residuals: the doc's >=30 percent cold-wall target needs the sanctioned Linux/LLVM lane + artifact-identity decisions; vendored-manifest feature alignment reported as a patch design for the cargo/seed-fix lane. close_evidence reproducer=scripts/bootstrap/tests/driver-watch-root-gate-test.shs prevention=src/compiler_rust/driver/build.rs"

